<BaseLayout title="Frequently asked questions — FreeMCP" description="Answers about MCP servers, FreeMCP listings, submissions, safety, and sponsorship.">
<article class="container info-page"><div class="eyebrow">FREEMCP / INFORMATION</div><h1>Frequently asked questions</h1><p class="intro">Answers about MCP servers, FreeMCP listings, submissions, safety, and sponsorship.</p><div class="info-content"><h2>What is MCP?</h2><p>The Model Context Protocol is an open protocol for connecting AI applications with external tools and data sources. See our <a href="/guides/what-is-mcp/">beginner's guide</a>.</p><h2>Is FreeMCP free?</h2><p>Browsing the public directory and proposing a listing are free. Sponsorships are optional promotional placements, not a requirement for submission.</p><h2>How do I submit a server?</h2><p>Use <a href="/submit/">Submit a server</a> with a public GitHub repository. The form prepares a GitHub issue for manual review; submission does not guarantee publication.</p><h2>Does FreeMCP verify servers?</h2><p>FreeMCP reviews available project evidence, but listings are not independent security certifications. Check source code, permissions, dependencies, and maintainer documentation before installing anything.</p><h2>How can I correct or remove a listing?</h2><p>Open an <a href="https://github.com/strbbrn/freemcp-registry/issues">issue in the registry repository</a> with the listing URL and the requested correction.</p><h2>Does FreeMCP host the MCP servers?</h2><p>No. The directory links to projects maintained by their respective authors. Hosting and operation depend on each server's documentation.</p><h2>How can I sponsor FreeMCP?</h2><p>See the <a href="/#sponsor">sponsorship options</a> or contact <a href="mailto:agents@freemcp.in">agents@freemcp.in</a>.</p></div></article>
</BaseLayout>
